# Phase 3 Integration Guide - Compatible User System

## What Phase 3 Actually Does

Phase 3 takes your existing user management code and organizes it into clean, modular components WITHOUT changing how authentication works. Your session-based system remains intact.

## Files Created

### Core Models:
- `models/User.js` - Handles all user data operations with your existing structure
- `models/PendingUser.js` - Manages pending user approval workflow
- `models/PendingDeletion.js` - Handles deletion request workflow

### Controllers:
- `controllers/userController.js` - Contains all user business logic
- `controllers/deletionController.js` - Manages deletion requests

### Routes:
- `routes/users.js` - All user-related endpoints
- `routes/deletions.js` - Deletion request endpoints

### Test File:
- `test-users-phase3-compatible.js` - Comprehensive testing

## Installation Steps

### Step 1: Create Directory Structure
```bash
mkdir models controllers
```

### Step 2: Add the Files
Copy all the Phase 3 files into your project.

### Step 3: Install Missing Dependencies (if needed)
```bash
npm install uuid
```

### Step 4: Run the Test
```bash
node test-users-phase3-compatible.js
```

### Step 5: Update server.js
Add these lines to your server.js:

```javascript
// Add to imports section
const userRoutes = require('./routes/users');
const deletionRoutes = require('./routes/deletions');

// Add after your existing middleware
app.use(userRoutes);
app.use(deletionRoutes);
```

### Step 6: Remove Old Code
Delete these sections from your server.js (they're now in the modules):
- All `/users*` route handlers
- All `/pendingUsers*` route handlers
- All `/pendingDeletions*` route handlers
- All `/login`, `/logout` route handlers
- All `/check-username`, `/check-email` handlers
- All `/verify-session` handlers

